## 8. Variables d'environnement (mirror Nexus)

| Variable | Valeur (exemple) | Effet |
|---|---|---|
| `ELECTRON_MIRROR` | `https://nexus.local/repository/github/electron/electron/releases/download/` | URL = `ELECTRON_MIRROR` + `v<VERSION>` + `/` + fichier. **Slash final obligatoire** |
| `ELECTRON_BUILDER_BINARIES_MIRROR` | `https://nexus.local/repository/github/electron-userland/electron-builder-binaries/releases/download/` | URL = mirror + `<release>/` + fichier (slash ajouté si absent) |
| `ELECTRON_BUILDER_BINARIES_ALLOW_HTTP` | `true` | uniquement si Nexus est en HTTP (HTTPS exigé sinon) |
| `ELECTRON_BUILDER_CACHE` | chemin **absolu** | cache des toolsets |
| `XDG_CACHE_HOME` | `$CI_PROJECT_DIR/.cache` | Linux : place `electron/` et `electron-builder/` dans le projet → cache GitLab simple |

À **ne pas** définir : `ELECTRON_BUILDER_BINARIES_CUSTOM_DIR` (remplace le segment `<release>` pour **tous** les toolsets).

Équivalent `.npmrc` (lu via `npm_config_*`) :

```ini
electron_mirror=https://nexus.local/repository/github/electron/electron/releases/download/
electron_builder_binaries_mirror=https://nexus.local/repository/github/electron-userland/electron-builder-binaries/releases/download/
```

Caches par défaut :

| OS | Electron | Toolsets electron-builder |
|---|---|---|
| Linux | `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/electron` ou `~/.cache/electron` | `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/electron-builder` ou `~/.cache/electron-builder` |
| Windows | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\electron\Cache` | `%LOCALAPPDATA%\electron-builder\Cache` |

